{
  "info": {
    "name": "Enjoy · Eventos e Inscripciones",
    "description": "API REST del gimnasio Enjoy — Proyecto integrador de Programación Backend II (CoderHouse).\n\nLa carpeta **Flujo completo** recorre los 11 casos del checklist de la entrega final en orden: ejecutala con el Collection Runner y cada request va dejando en las variables lo que necesita la siguiente (ids de eventos, tickets, etc.).\n\nLa autenticación viaja en la cookie HttpOnly `currentUser`, que Postman guarda solo si el jar de cookies está habilitado. Como cada rol necesita su propia sesión, las carpetas hacen login antes de las requests que lo requieren.\n\n**Variables**\n- `baseUrl`: raíz de la API (por defecto `http://localhost:8080/api`)\n- `userEmail` / `organizerEmail` / `otherOrganizerEmail` / `adminEmail` / `password`: credenciales de prueba\n\nAntes de correr el flujo: levantá el servidor (`npm run dev`) y promové los roles con `npm run set-role -- <email> <rol>` (ver README).",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "variable": [
    {
      "key": "baseUrl",
      "value": "http://localhost:8080/api"
    },
    {
      "key": "password",
      "value": "Secreta123"
    },
    {
      "key": "userEmail",
      "value": "lucia@enjoy.com"
    },
    {
      "key": "organizerEmail",
      "value": "martin@enjoy.com"
    },
    {
      "key": "otherOrganizerEmail",
      "value": "sofia@enjoy.com"
    },
    {
      "key": "adminEmail",
      "value": "ana@enjoy.com"
    },
    {
      "key": "eventId",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "ticketId",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "userId",
      "value": ""
    }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "Flujo completo (checklist de la entrega final)",
      "description": "Los 11 casos verificados en `npm run e2e`, en el mismo orden. Correr con el Collection Runner de arriba hacia abajo.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "01 · Registro (201, sin password)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('201 Created', () => pm.response.to.have.status(201));",
                  "pm.test('no expone password', () => pm.expect(JSON.stringify(body)).to.not.include('password'));",
                  "pm.test('devuelve rol user', () => pm.expect(body.payload.role).to.eql('user'));",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('userId', body.payload.id);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/sessions/register",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "sessions",
                "register"
              ]
            },
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"first_name\": \"Lucia\",\n  \"last_name\": \"Pereyra\",\n  \"email\": \"{{userEmail}}\",\n  \"password\": \"{{password}}\"\n}"
            },
            "description": "El rol nunca se toma del body: aunque mandes `\"role\": \"admin\"`, el usuario se crea como `user`."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "02 · Login user (200 + cookie HttpOnly)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('200 OK', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const cookie = pm.response.headers.get('set-cookie') || '';",
                  "pm.test('cookie currentUser HttpOnly', () => {",
                  "  pm.expect(cookie).to.include('currentUser=');",
                  "  pm.expect(cookie.toLowerCase()).to.include('httponly');",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/sessions/login",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "sessions",
                "login"
              ]
            },
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"{{userEmail}}\",\n  \"password\": \"{{password}}\"\n}"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "03 · /current con sesión (200, perfil completo)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('200 OK', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.test('perfil completo', () => pm.expect(body.payload).to.have.all.keys('id', 'first_name', 'last_name', 'email', 'role'));",
                  "pm.test('sin password', () => pm.expect(JSON.stringify(body)).to.not.include('password'));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/sessions/current",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "sessions",
                "current"
              ]
            },
            "description": "El perfil se relee de la base en cada llamada, así refleja un cambio de rol posterior al login."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "04 · user intenta crear evento (403)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('403 Forbidden', () => pm.response.to.have.status(403));",
                  "pm.test('mensaje de permisos', () => pm.expect(pm.response.json().message).to.include('permisos'));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/events",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "events"
              ]
            },
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"title\": \"Clase pirata\",\n  \"description\": \"Un user no puede crear eventos\",\n  \"category\": \"clase\",\n  \"date\": \"{{$isoTimestamp}}\",\n  \"location\": \"Sede Centro\",\n  \"capacity\": 10\n}"
            },
            "description": "Autenticado pero sin el rol requerido: 403, no 401."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "05 · Logout y /current sin sesión (401)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "prerequest",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "// Cerramos sesión antes de pedir /current para comprobar el 401.",
                  "pm.sendRequest({",
                  "  url: pm.collectionVariables.get('baseUrl') + '/sessions/logout',",
                  "  method: 'POST',",
                  "}, () => {});"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('401 Unauthorized', () => pm.response.to.have.status(401));",
                  "pm.test('mensaje No autenticado', () => pm.expect(pm.response.json().message).to.eql('No autenticado'));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/sessions/current",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "sessions",
                "current"
              ]
            },
            "description": "El pre-request hace el logout; esta request comprueba que la cookie ya no sirve."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "06 · Login organizer",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('200 OK', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.test('el organizer existe y tiene el rol', () => pm.expect(pm.response.code).to.eql(200));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/sessions/login",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "sessions",
                "login"
              ]
            },
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"{{organizerEmail}}\",\n  \"password\": \"{{password}}\"\n}"
            },
            "description": "Requiere haber corrido `npm run set-role -- {{organizerEmail}} organizer`."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "07 · organizer crea evento (201)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "prerequest",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "// Fecha futura: 15 días a partir de ahora.",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('futureDate', new Date(Date.now() + 15 * 86400000).toISOString());"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('201 Created', () => pm.response.to.have.status(201));",
                  "pm.test('status published', () => pm.expect(body.payload.status).to.eql('published'));",
                  "pm.test('capacity 2', () => pm.expect(body.payload.capacity).to.eql(2));",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('eventId', body.payload.id);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/events",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "events"
              ]
            },
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"title\": \"Funcional al aire libre\",\n  \"description\": \"Entrenamiento funcional en el parque\",\n  \"category\": \"clase\",\n  \"date\": \"{{futureDate}}\",\n  \"location\": \"Parque Sarmiento\",\n  \"capacity\": 2,\n  \"price\": 4500\n}"
            },
            "description": "Cupo chico (2) a propósito, para poder probar el agotamiento de cupo más adelante."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "08 · user se inscribe (201 + email)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "prerequest",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "// Volvemos a la sesión del user.",
                  "pm.sendRequest({",
                  "  url: pm.collectionVariables.get('baseUrl') + '/sessions/login',",
                  "  method: 'POST',",
                  "  header: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },",
                  "  body: { mode: 'raw', raw: JSON.stringify({ email: pm.collectionVariables.get('userEmail'), password: pm.collectionVariables.get('password') }) },",
                  "}, () => {});"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('201 Created', () => pm.response.to.have.status(201));",
                  "pm.test('status confirmed', () => pm.expect(body.payload.status).to.eql('confirmed'));",
                  "pm.test('tiene código de reserva', () => pm.expect(body.payload.reservationCode).to.match(/^ENJ-/));",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('ticketId', body.payload.id);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/events/{{eventId}}/tickets",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "events",
                "{{eventId}}",
                "tickets"
              ]
            },
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"quantity\": 1\n}"
            },
            "description": "Si las variables MAIL_* están configuradas, se envía el email de confirmación (con Ethereal, el link de vista previa aparece en la consola del servidor). `quantity` es opcional y vale 1 por defecto."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "09 · Inscripción duplicada (409)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('409 Conflict', () => pm.response.to.have.status(409));",
                  "pm.test('mensaje de duplicado', () => pm.expect(pm.response.json().message).to.include('inscripción activa'));",
                  "pm.test('error de negocio, no 500', () => pm.expect(pm.response.code).to.not.eql(500));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/events/{{eventId}}/tickets",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "events",
                "{{eventId}}",
                "tickets"
              ]
            },
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{}"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "10 · Cupo insuficiente (409)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('409 Conflict', () => pm.response.to.have.status(409));",
                  "pm.test('mensaje claro de cupos', () => pm.expect(pm.response.json().message).to.match(/cupos/i));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/events/{{eventId}}/tickets",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "events",
                "{{eventId}}",
                "tickets"
              ]
            },
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"quantity\": 50\n}"
            },
            "description": "Pide más lugares de los que quedan. El mensaje indica cuántos hay disponibles."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "11 · Mis tickets (200, populate sin password)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('200 OK', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.test('el evento viene populado y filtrado', () => {",
                  "  pm.expect(body.payload[0].event).to.have.all.keys('id', 'title', 'date', 'location', 'status');",
                  "});",
                  "pm.test('sin password', () => pm.expect(JSON.stringify(body)).to.not.include('password'));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/tickets/my-tickets",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "tickets",
                "my-tickets"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Solo los tickets propios. El populate del evento está filtrado por el DTO `toMyTicket`."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "12 · Cancelar ticket propio (200, libera cupo)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('200 OK', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.test('status cancelled', () => pm.expect(body.payload.status).to.eql('cancelled'));",
                  "pm.test('registra cancelledAt', () => pm.expect(body.payload.cancelledAt).to.not.be.null);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "PATCH",
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/tickets/{{ticketId}}/cancel",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "tickets",
                "{{ticketId}}",
                "cancel"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Cancelación lógica: el ticket no se borra, cambia de estado y deja de ocupar cupo."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "13 · organizer ajeno intenta modificar (403)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "prerequest",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "// Entramos con el OTRO organizer, que no es dueño del evento.",
                  "pm.sendRequest({",
                  "  url: pm.collectionVariables.get('baseUrl') + '/sessions/login',",
                  "  method: 'POST',",
                  "  header: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },",
                  "  body: { mode: 'raw', raw: JSON.stringify({ email: pm.collectionVariables.get('otherOrganizerEmail'), password: pm.collectionVariables.get('password') }) },",
                  "}, () => {});"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('403 Forbidden', () => pm.response.to.have.status(403));",
                  "pm.test('no es 404: el evento existe, falta el permiso', () => pm.expect(pm.response.code).to.eql(403));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "PUT",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/events/{{eventId}}",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "events",
                "{{eventId}}"
              ]
            },
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"title\": \"Evento secuestrado\"\n}"
            },
            "description": "Requiere `npm run set-role -- {{otherOrganizerEmail}} organizer`. Tiene el rol pero no es dueño del recurso."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "14 · admin modifica evento ajeno (200)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "prerequest",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.sendRequest({",
                  "  url: pm.collectionVariables.get('baseUrl') + '/sessions/login',",
                  "  method: 'POST',",
                  "  header: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },",
                  "  body: { mode: 'raw', raw: JSON.stringify({ email: pm.collectionVariables.get('adminEmail'), password: pm.collectionVariables.get('password') }) },",
                  "}, () => {});"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('200 OK', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.test('título actualizado', () => pm.expect(pm.response.json().payload.title).to.include('admin'));"
                ]
              }
